From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flax <flax@tiogapass>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbtp: add missing Labels allowlist to the PCH VR

Every pmbus block in fbtp.json carries a "Labels" allowlist naming the
hwmon labels psusensor should expose - except MB_VR_PCH_PVNN /
MB_VR_PCH_P1V05 at 0x68.  Without it psusensor instantiates *every*
in*_input on the chip, including the 12 V input rails vin1/vin2, and two
upstream dbus-sensors defects then combine to bind the wrong file:

  1. PSUSensorMain.cpp:676 looks the hwmon label up in labelMatch, but
     that table is keyed "vin"/"vout" while the label file says "vin1"/
     "vout1".  The lookup misses and both fall back to labelMatch["in"]
     = PSUProperty("Output Voltage", 255, 0, 3, 0), so vin1 and vout1
     compose the *identical* sensor name "MB_VR_PCH_PVNN Output Voltage"
     (and vin2/vout2 collide on MB_VR_PCH_P1V05).

  2. On a host power-on the daemon re-scans with activateOnly=true
     (PSUSensorMain.cpp:1149) and PSUSensor::activate() early-returns on
     an already-active sensor, so the *first* file in readdir order wins.
     On this board readdir yields in2,in5,in3,in6,in1,in4 - the vin
     files come first, and the vout rebind is silently discarded.

The sensor therefore reads the 12 V input rail while keeping vout1's
1.1 V critical threshold, and asserts "Upper Critical going high,
Reading 12 > Threshold 1 Volts" on both rails at every host power-on,
deasserting only at power-off.  The PCH rails themselves are fine
(vout1 = 1.000 V, vout2 = 1.050 V, confirmed against the independent
ADC sensors MB_PVNN_PCH_STBY and MB_P1V05).

Give 0x68 the same allowlist the other dual-output VRs (0x48, 0x58)
already have.  The vin files are then skipped at PSUSensorMain.cpp:663,
there is no name collision left to lose the race on, and the sensors
bind to vout1/vout2 as intended.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform configuration]
---
 configurations/fbtp.json | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/configurations/fbtp.json
+++ b/configurations/fbtp.json
@@ -1299,6 +1299,16 @@
     {
       "Address": "0x68",
       "Bus": 5,
+      "Labels": [
+        "iout1",
+        "iout2",
+        "pout1",
+        "pout2",
+        "vout1",
+        "vout2",
+        "temp1",
+        "temp2"
+      ],
       "Name": "MB_VR_PCH_PVNN",
       "Name1": "MB_VR_PCH_P1V05",
       "Thresholds": [
